  "sections": [
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "hero",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -2,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1080,
      "heading": "Agents check the code. Humans judge the idea.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Nebius × NVIDIA Global AI Hackathon entry ↗",
        "Get started",
        "Read the docs"
      ],
      "text": "Nebius × NVIDIA Global AI Hackathon entry ↗ Agents check the code. Humans judge the idea. Coding agents turned 100 hand-coded submissions into 1,000. RoundOne’s judging agent, NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius, builds every repo, watches every demo and visits every live site. Your judges get their attention back for the part that matters. Get started Read the docs",
      "layout": "split",
      "assetUrls": [
        "http://roundone.localhost:3001/_next/image?url=%2Flanding%2Fretro-hero.webp&w=1920&q=75"
      ]
    },
    {
      "selector": "#shift",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 1449,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 1129,
      "heading": "Building got cheap. Judging didn't.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "THE NEW NORMAL Building got cheap. Judging didn't. When a weekend team can ship a working app with a coding agent, “does it run?” stops separating the field. What separates projects now is what a person brought: the problem they picked, the insight, the taste. Ten times the pile, same three judges Submissions multiplied. The panel didn’t. At a careful eight minutes a look, 1,000 projects is 400 judge-hours, and in practice nobody runs the code. The projects at the bottom of the pile get the tired judges. ~100 hand-coded, before coding agents 1,000+ agent-assisted, now. Nearly all of them run. ",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#split",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 2578,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 1596,
      "heading": "Let the machine check the machine.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Nebius × NVIDIA Devpost page"
      ],
      "text": "THE SPLIT Let the machine check the machine. Save people for what people made. The agent takes every criterion a machine can verify, and the ones only people can score stay with your judges. The agent checks Does it build and pass its tests? Does it use the sponsor tech? Does the demo match the claims? Did it follow the rules? Humans judge Is the idea new? Would it matter to anyone? Is it made with taste? Would you use it? RoundOne can judge the hackathon it’s entered in Every submission rule on the Nebius × NVIDIA Devpost page can run as a must-pass gate: the repo builds, it calls Token Facto",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#fatigue",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 4174,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 1654,
      "heading": "A queue a person can actually finish",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "JUDGE FATIGUE A queue a person can actually finish Built for the judge on project forty, not project one. Batch the work, screen out the noise and keep every score a person's own. One link. Today's batch. A time estimate. Each judge gets a private page with today's projects, what they'll score and about how long it'll take. Then it walks them through one project at a time. AI Global AI Hackathon 4/12 GH ROUND 1 · DAY 2 OF 5 Welcome, Grace 4 of 12 done today, 8 to go. 36 more open over the coming days. Keep going About 32 minutes · each score saves when you submit it Your projects today #118 Ti",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#control",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 5828,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 1460,
      "heading": "The agent does the homework. People make the call.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "HUMANS IN THE LOOP The agent does the homework. People make the call. Judges' average scores set the ranking. The agent's score only breaks ties, and it never picks a winner. 01 Setup You Write the rubric and the agent's guidance in your own words. Keep any criterion human only. Agent Learns what to look for, criterion by criterion. 02 Screening You Rule on the projects the agent fails on a gate. Agent Checks every project against your gates and shows its evidence. 03 Judging You Score first, then compare. Gaps of 2 points or more get flagged. Agent Scores what it can check, with its reasoning",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#stack",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7288,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1097,
      "heading": "Open models, on infrastructure you own",
      "backgroundColor": "#150C2E",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "OPEN STACK Open models, on infrastructure you own The judging agent runs on open models and open infrastructure, from the first build check to the last prior-art search. EVERY VERDICT Nemotron Pick how much model each criterion gets. Every tier is Nemotron. QUICK Nemotron 3.5 Lightning One fast pass over what the mechanisms found BALANCED Nemotron 3 Super 120B Checks a few things itself with tools. Also runs the chat IN-DEPTH Nemotron 3 Ultra 550B The largest model, with room to dig Double check: when the agent is unsure, a larger Nemotron takes a second look. INFERENCE AND SANDBOXES Token Fac",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#features",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 8385,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 2264,
      "heading": "One place from setup to winners",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Read the docs →",
        "Docs →"
      ],
      "text": "EVERYTHING ELSE One place from setup to winners Describe what teams submit and how each criterion gets checked, run the rounds, then announce the winners. 01 Setup Describe what teams submit, what projects are scored on and how each criterion is checked. Add judges and plan the rounds. Schema Criteria Judges Phases 02 Judging The agent reviews every project. Judges work through private queues. You watch each round fill in and close it when it's done. Projects Progress Inbox Chat 03 Results Review the final ranking, pick award winners, email them what they won and publish the winners page. Winn",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#self-host",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 384,
      "y": 10649,
      "width": 1152,
      "height": 648,
      "heading": "Run it on your own stack",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Deployment guide"
      ],
      "text": "SELF-HOSTED Run it on your own stack RoundOne is a Next.js app on Supabase. Deploy it for your org, choose the models the agent runs on and put your name, color and logo on every page from one config file. Your brand on the app, the judge portal and the winners page Submissions and scores stay in your own database Documented end to end, down to every page and API Deployment guide // branding.config.js const branding = { name: \"Acme Hacks\", badge: \"AH\", logo: \"/logo.svg\", color: \"#ff5a1f\", }; // .env.local: swap the model behind any tier NEBIUS_QUICK_MODEL=\"nvidia/Nemotron-3_5-Lightning\" NEBIUS",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 512,
      "y": 11297,
      "width": 896,
      "height": 588,
      "heading": "Give your judges their attention back",
      "backgroundColor": "#150C2E",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Get started",
        "Quickstart"
      ],
      "text": "Give your judges their attention back Let the agent run the checks on every project. Your judges spend their time on the ideas. Get started Quickstart",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    }
